    "created_at": "2017-09-25T23:10:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-25T23:11:08Z",
    "body": "(It took me quite a while to recall what I was thinking when I made that comment. Although I'm not completely sure, but I think it is what I was considering:)\r\n\r\nThe problem is unrelated to hierarchy restrictions. It is more about that whether a `<dialog>` can go fullscreen. If a `<dialog>` itself can go fullscreen, then HTML spec removing it from top layer may pose unexpected result in various algorithms when the `<dialog>` is in fullscreen.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why you don't want to merge #91 (probably because of lack of test at the moment?), but if that's troublesome to merge, probably we can move the single restriction on `<dialog>` element to a new PR and land it separately to resolve this specific problem.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
